      <div class='homelab'>
      <h2>AI Consensus Prototype <small>Dec 2025</small></h2>

      <h2 id='what'>What it is</h2>
      <p><strong>ai-consensus-poc</strong> is a prototype built in December 2025. A Go <em>brain</em> service takes a prompt, uses Claude to break it into subtasks, and fans those subtasks out to a pool of <em>child</em> Claude agents. The children are a single Kubernetes Deployment, so adding more is a matter of scaling its replicas. Each child sends its answer back to the brain, which reviews the results and either synthesizes a final answer or sends out refined questions for another round. It keeps iterating until the children reach consensus, capped at 10 iterations.</p>

      <h2 id='consensus'>How consensus works</h2>
      <p>The brain does not wait for every child. It waits for a <strong>quorum</strong>: a majority of the children it handed subtasks to that round must respond before it moves on. It then runs a 4-step analysis over the responses:</p>
      <ol style='text-align:left'>
        <li><strong>Identify claims</strong> - pull the key claims out of each child's response</li>
        <li><strong>Compare agreement</strong> - check how far those claims line up across children</li>
        <li><strong>Evaluate consensus strength</strong> - grade it as strong consensus, weak consensus or no consensus</li>
        <li><strong>Decide the next step</strong> - synthesize the final answer, or write refined questions that target the disagreements and start another iteration</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id='architecture'>Architecture</h2>
<pre style='text-align:left;display:inline-block;font-size:12px;line-height:1.3;'>
                  prompt
                    |
                    v
       +-------------------------+
       |          BRAIN          |&lt;-----------------------+
       |  1. plan subtasks       |                        |
       |  2. wait for quorum     |                        |
       |  3. review: 4-step      |                        |
       |     consensus analysis  |                        |
       +------------+------------+                        |
                    |  subtasks                           |
      +-------------+-------------+-------------+         |
      |             |             |             |         |
      v             v             v             v         |
 +---------+   +---------+   +---------+   +---------+    |
 | child-1 |   | child-2 |   | child-3 |...| child-N |    |
 +----+----+   +----+----+   +----+----+   +----+----+    |
      |             |             |             |         |
      +-------------+------+------+-------------+         |
                           |                              |
                           +---- results -----------------+

        no consensus yet? refined questions go back out
        (at most 10 iterations), otherwise final answer
</pre>

      <h2 id='stack'>Stack</h2>
      <ul class='sub' style='text-align:left'>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Go services</strong> - a <em>brain</em> orchestrator and a <em>child</em> agent service, calling Claude through the Anthropic Go SDK</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Event bus</strong> - an internal bus that broadcasts messages, node and edge updates, task start and end, and iteration events</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>WebSocket hub</strong> - streams those events live to the dashboard</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>React dashboard</strong> - an IRC-style communication log next to a neural-network graph view of the brain and its children</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Per-child model selection</strong> - click a child node in the graph to pick which Claude model it runs</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Kubernetes</strong> - manifests for the brain, the child Deployment and the dashboard</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>SOPS</strong> - secrets kept encrypted in the repo</li>
      </ul>

